# Durchkriechstein (Schliefstein) beside the Falkensteinkirche, back-layer
# prop (D-057): a rounded limestone boulder 4 tiles wide and 3 tall. Rows
# 0-31 = the boulder over the level's invisible solid tiles (drawn = solid,
# D-038): its top is row 0 (the corners round off by <= 2 px over the first
# 6 px), i body with a w highlight at the top left and a w lip, m shade
# with a curved terminator in the right quarter and a curved m underside,
# m cracks, two m cup marks (the saint's and the devil's traces), g/G moss.
# Rows 32-47 = the low tunnel (the empty tile row): an irregular arched
# ceiling (rows 31-33, radius-3 corners at the mouths, a dip near the
# middle, >= 14 clear rows above the floor) with a broken k shadow line,
# the boulder resting on two rounded 3-5 px feet (lit w/i left, m right,
# polished mouth edges), d interior, a lighter m/i patch where the far
# opening lets the light in, worn m floor stones. Resi is drawn over it
# while crawling. No outline (back layer). Drawn by the pixel-artist with a
# throwaway script; the grid is the source.
sprite = durchkriechstein
size   = 64x48
origin = 32,48
anim   = idle frames=1
---
frame idle 0
